# What does NOT get uploaded when the phone app is built.
#
# Read this before changing it. It is not a duplicate of .gitignore.
#
# `eas build` sends a copy of this repository to Expo's build servers. When
# this file exists, EAS uses it and ignores every .gitignore in the project —
# all of them, at every level. So anything that must not leave this machine has
# to be listed here as well, and a line deleted from here is a file uploaded.
#
# Why it exists at all
# --------------------
# `dwell app` writes the course server's address into app/.env, and .gitignore
# excludes that file — correctly, since the address belongs to one course and
# not in a public repository. But EAS honoured the same rule, so the address
# never reached the build, and the app that came back said it had not been set
# up. The URL is baked into the bundle at build time, so there is no later
# opportunity to supply it: an app built without it is simply an app that
# collects nothing.
#
# This file is that exception, made explicitly and in one place, rather than by
# loosening .gitignore and risking the address being committed.
#
# The one rule when editing this: app/.env stays uploaded, and everything under
# data/local/ stays out.

# ---- must never leave this machine ----------------------------------------
# The course database (participant coordinates), the key that signs instructor
# sign-ins, and participant device tokens all live here.
data/local/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Contains this course's secret key and a bundle of the server.
deploy/

# May contain paths and configuration from this installation.
support-report.txt

# Every .env EXCEPT app/.env, which is the whole point of this file.
.env
.env.*
!app/.env
!.env.example

# ---- not needed by the build ----------------------------------------------
.git/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.metro-health-check*

# Native projects are generated by the build, not carried into it.
app/ios/
app/android/
.kotlin/
*.orig.*

# Signing material. Nothing here should ever hold any, and if something does,
# it should not be posted to a build server by accident.
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
*.mobileprovision

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
